   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["ReplaceSpinorZ", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Replaces a two-index auxiliary z object in a supported massive \
shift.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ReplaceSpinorZ", "[", "expr", ",",
         " ", "{", "i", ",", " ", "mi", "}", ",", " ", "{", "j", ",", " ",
         "mj", "}", ",", " ", "k", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "rewrites \
SpinorZ[\"Both\",I,J] when both specified masses are nonzero."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The result is a sum of a massive \
spinor bracket and a chain with Mom[k], divided by mi mj. The original \
upper/lower little-group indices are retained.", "Notes"],
  Cell["If either mass is zero, this particular replacement is not applied. \
It is not a generic rule for all SpinorZ forms.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
